Third-Party Data Sources
------------------------

### OpenSky Network (ADS-B flight data)

This project uses data from the OpenSky Network (https://opensky-network.org/).
Use of OpenSky data is restricted to non-commercial and research purposes under
their Terms of Use (https://opensky-network.org/about/terms-of-use).

Academic and research use of OpenSky data should cite:

  Matthias Schafer, Martin Strohmeier, Vincent Lenders, Ivan Martinovic, Matthias Wilhelm.
  "Bringing Up OpenSky: A Large-scale ADS-B Sensor Network for Research."
  In Proceedings of the 13th IEEE/ACM International Symposium on Information Processing
  in Sensor Networks (IPSN), pages 83-94, April 2014.

This project does not redistribute OpenSky data. It queries the live API at runtime
for the sole purpose of demonstrating distributed systems architecture.

### AISHub (AIS vessel data)

This project references AISHub (https://www.aishub.net/) as a potential AIS data source.
AISHub operates on a contribution model - users are expected to contribute AIS receiver
data in exchange for API access. Verify eligibility with AISHub before connecting a
live feed. This project does not redistribute AISHub data.
